{"result":{"biographic_references":[],"contributors":{"authors":[{"aliases":[],"checked":"1","codes":["harborth.heiko"],"name":"Harborth, Heiko"},{"aliases":[],"checked":"0","codes":["krause.stefan"],"name":"Krause, Stefan"}],"author_references":[],"editors":[]},"database":"Zbl","datestamp":"2004-06-22T12:36:35Z","document_type":{"code":"j","description":"journal article"},"editorial_contributions":[{"language":"English","reviewer":{"author_code":"faudree.ralph-j","reviewer_id":"3352","name":"Ralph Faudree","sign":"Ralph Faudree (Memphis)"},"text":"A \\(2\\)-coloring of the diagonals (including sides) of a regular convex \\(n\\)-gon is a circulant coloring of \\(K_n\\) if all diagonals of the same length have the same color. Corresponding to such colorings are two circulant Ramsey numbers \\(RC_1(G,H)\\) and \\(RC_2(G,H)\\) such that for all \\(n < RC_1(G,H)\\) a circulant coloring without a monochromatic \\(G\\) or \\(H\\) exists and for all \\(n \\geq RC_2\\) no such coloring exists. The Ramsey numbers \\(RC_1\\) and \\(RC_2\\) are determined for all paths, cycles, graphs on at most five vertices, and for some small complete graphs. As a consequence of the latter results, new lower bounds \\(R(K_4,K_{10}) \\geq 92\\) and \\(R(K_5,K_8) \\geq 101\\) for classical Ramsey numbers are obtained.","contribution_type":"review"}],"id":2076935,"identifier":"1049.05056","keywords":["colorings","Ramsey numbers","circulant"],"language":{"languages":["English"],"addition":[null]},"license":[],"links":[{"identifier":"A267296","type":"oeis","url":"https://oeis.org/A267296"}],"msc":[{"code":"05C55","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Generalized Ramsey theory"},{"code":"05C15","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Coloring of graphs and hypergraphs"}],"references":[],"source":{"book":[],"pages":"139-150","series":[{"acronym":null,"issn":[{"number":"0384-9864","type":"print"}],"issue":null,"issue_id":103917,"parallel_title":null,"part":null,"publisher":"Combinatorial Press, Winnipeg, MB","series_id":1993,"short_title":"Congr. Numerantium","title":"Congressus Numerantium","volume":"161","year":"2003"}],"source":"Congr. Numerantium 161, 139-150 (2003)."},"states":[["o","has open version"],["c","is cited"]],"title":{"addition":null,"original":null,"subtitle":null,"title":"Ramsey numbers for circulant colorings"},"year":"2003","zbmath_url":"https://zbmath.org/2076935"},"status":{"execution":"successful request","execution_bool":true,"internal_code":"ok","last_id":null,"nr_total_results":1,"nr_request_results":1,"query_execution_time_in_seconds":0.046998023986816406,"status_code":200,"time_stamp":"2026-11-08T01:13:01Z"}}